title: "Collatz matrix obstructions, synchronization, and basin densities"
authors:
  - family-names: Valbuena
    given-names: Lucas
repository-code: "https://github.com/x1xhlol/collatz-two-coordinate-obstruction"
url: "https://github.com/x1xhlol/collatz-two-coordinate-obstruction"
abstract: >-
  Three standalone papers and accompanying Lean proofs. The first establishes
  two-coordinate affine interpretation obstructions for the Yolcu–Aaronson–Heule
  Collatz system. The second gives an independent proof of Said Duran's
  equal-height runs theorem, with priority credited to his earlier preprint.
  The third derives logarithmic basin densities and canonical trace limits
  from Tao's first-passage stabilization. Additional results of Mazur give
  natural-density limits and positivity at targets prime to three. Its Lean
  formalization currently covers selected proof steps, not the full analytic
  theorem chain. None of the papers proves the Collatz conjecture.
keywords:
  - Collatz conjecture
  - string rewriting
  - matrix interpretations
  - Lean
  - formal verification
  - natural density
  - logarithmic density
  - first passage
